# Post-Edit Verification

`AGENTS.md` is the workflow source of truth.

## Ableton sync (non-negotiable — do this last, do not skip)

After **any** substantive change to the device—`ghq_*.js`, `guitar-hq.maxpat`, `Guitar-HQ.amxd`, or `scripts/build-device-patch.js` / `scripts/sync-user-library.js`—you **must** run:

```sh
node scripts/sync-user-library.js
```

**Do not finish the task without a successful sync.** Live reads `.js` from the User Library folder, not the git working tree.

**Synced files:** `ghq_engine.js`, `ghq_compact_ui.js`, `ghq_editor_ui.js`, `ghq_ui_shared.js`, `ghq_rack_map.js`, `Guitar-HQ.amxd`

**Default destination (macOS):**

`~/Music/Ableton/User Library/Presets/Audio Effects/Max Audio Effect/`

Override with **`GHQ_ABLETON_DEST`** (not `KSH_ABLETON_DEST`).

**While developing:** `npm run sync:watch` debounces copies on save.

`node scripts/build-device-patch.js` also syncs at the end; if you **only** changed `.js` files, run sync explicitly anyway.

## Tests and patch checks

| What changed | Run before finishing |
|--------------|----------------------|
| `ghq_rack_map.js` or `ghq_rack_map.test.js` | `node ghq_rack_map.test.js` |
| `ghq_engine.js`, UIs, or `ghq_ui_shared.js` | `node --check <each changed .js>` or `npm test` |
| Any device file above | `node scripts/validate-device-patch.js` |
| `guitar-hq.maxpat` or `scripts/build-device-patch.js` | `node scripts/build-device-patch.js` then `node scripts/validate-device-patch.js` |
| **Always** (device edits) | **`node scripts/sync-user-library.js`** |

Fix failures before finishing. `npm run verify` = build + test + validate (build includes sync); explicit commands above still apply when you did not run full verify.

## Substantive vs trivial

- **Substantive:** logic, UI, rack map, patch wiring, generated `.amxd`, scripts under `scripts/`, anything affecting Live behavior.
- **Trivial (sync still required if device files touched):** comment-only edits in `ghq_*.js` still need sync if the user will reload in Live.

**Docs-only** (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules`) — no sync unless accompanied by device file changes.
